{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788264664,"nonce":"s7SlBWaBeyU3YFrvvV8Jni9uEtc=","message":"AMENDMENT — OUT-6 of the M1 post-mortem (`RUNS/m1-20260831/postmortem.md`). This spec's fight-over predicate could never have fired in the M1 run, and the reason generalises.\n\n**`threats.hostiles` was 6 or 7 for the ENTIRE run.** The map shipped an insect hive — 4 megascarab, a locust, a spelopede — fogged from tick 0, dormant, never approaching, and `pawns {filter:\"hostile\"}` read 0 for them the whole time. So any post-raid procedure predicated on \"hostiles reach zero\" was structurally unable to trigger on that map, from tick 1, regardless of what happened in the actual fight.\n\nThat is a structural root cause in `postmortem.md`'s taxonomy, not bad luck: an insect hive is ordinary map generation, and this spec's trigger silently does not exist on any map that has one.\n\n**Re-predicate fight-over on hostiles that are REACHABLE and NOT FOGGED**, rather than on the raw count. Evan's ruling of 2026-09-01 gives the vocabulary and the mechanism: a hostile the colony has deliberately declined to fight is *pardoned* — a journalled act with a required reason — and `digest.threats` now publishes `hostiles_pardoned` and `hostiles_unpardoned` beside an unchanged `hostiles` (verb `threat-pardon`, shipped this session). `hostiles_unpardoned` is the right input for this trigger, and it makes the \"we are not fighting those\" decision explicit and auditable instead of implicit in a predicate.\n\nWhether \"pardoned\" is sufficient or whether this spec also wants a live reachability/fog test is a real question — a pardon is a decision, reachability is a fact, and a hostile can be unpardoned and still unreachable. Decide it here and say which.\n\nOne line also owed in `checklists/turn.md` §hostiles-standing: a nonzero `hostiles` on a map with a hive is the normal resting state, and treating it as an active threat is what made `raid-end` unreachable.","files":null}]}